import FourColor.Discharge

/-!
# Hubcaps  (port of `hubcap.v`)

Ruling out a part using a combination of discharging and reducibility. In principle, this
brings together almost all the elements of the proof development, so for modularity we only
import a predicate `redp` on parts from the reducibility half, with the assumption that it is
always false when the part fits the map (Coq section hypothesis `redpP`). Everything is tied up
in `present.v` (`redp` will be the `redpart` predicate of `redpart.v`).

A hubcap is a list of constraints on the `dscore2` values around the hub: the constraint
`cons1 j b` means `dscore2 (face^j x) ≤ b`, and `cons2 j1 j2 b` means
`dscore2 (face^j1 x) + dscore2 (face^j2 x) ≤ b`. Indices start at 0 here, as in the Coq
constructors (the Coq concrete syntax `$[i] <= b` counts from 1, and the notation shifts the
indices down by 1). The concrete syntax (Coq module `HubcapSyntax`) is not ported, since the
presentation data is generated by a script.

The hubcap checking functions all assume a context with a fixed hub size `nhub` and a rule
fork `rf : DruleFork nhub` for that size; `rs0`, `rt0` (Coq section `Let`s) are the source and
target rules `rf.sourceDrules`, `rf.targetDrules` of that fork. There is also a reducibility
checking function `redp`, which we assume always returns `false` on a part fitting the
hypermap we consider (hypothesis `redpP`).

## Definitions (Coq name → Lean name)

* `hubcap` (constructors `Hubcap0`, `Hubcap1`, `Hubcap2`) → `Hubcap` (constructors `nil`,
  `cons1`, `cons2`).
* `check_dbound1 redp rf p ns` → `checkDbound1 redp rf p ns`: at most `ns` source rules in `rf`
  apply at a dart `x` that fits `p` (if `p` has size `nhub`): `dbound1 rs0 x ≤ ns`. It is not
  used to check hubcaps, but to get a global upper bound on score transfers across a given edge,
  in order to use `dscore_cap1` to handle hub sizes 12 and up in `unavoidability.v`.
* `check_dbound1_rec redp p rs ns m` → `checkDbound1Rec redp p rs ns m`: the recursive
  subpredicate for `checkDbound1`: `m` is a termination count, `p` the intersection of the
  initial part with some source rules assumed to match, `rs` the list of rules that overlap
  with `p` properly, and `ns` the strict bound on the number of rules in `rs` that can match
  implied by the original bound; we check `redp` holds whenever `ns` is reached.
* `check_unfit p ru` → `checkUnfit p ru`: part `p` implies one of the "excluded" rules in `ru`.
* `check_dbound2 redp rf p b` → `checkDbound2 redp rf p b`: the net score transfer for an `x`
  that fits part `p` (of size `nhub`), under the rules of `rf`, is at most `b : ℤ`; more
  precisely, `dbound2 rt0 rs0 x ≤ b`.
* `check_dbound2_rec redp p rt rs ru nt m` → `checkDbound2Rec redp p rt rs ru nt m`: the
  recursive subpredicate for `checkDbound2`; the parameters are as for `checkDbound1Rec`, except
  we now also keep track of target rules, the bound `nt` is for target rules, `p` is
  specialized according to target rules, and we keep track of the list `ru` of target rules that
  have been assumed NOT to match.
* `check_2dbound2 redp rf p i b` → `check2Dbound2 redp rf p i b`: the sum of the net score
  transfers for an `x` that fits part `p` (of size `nhub`), and for `y = face^i x`, is at most
  `b`: `dbound2 rt0 rs0 x + dbound2 rt0 rs0 y ≤ b`.
* `check_2dbound2_rec nhub redp p1 p2 rt1 rs1 ru1 rt2 rs2 ru2 i nt m` → `check2Dbound2Rec` (same
  arguments): the recursive subpredicate for `check2Dbound2`; the parameters are as for
  `checkDbound2Rec`, with both `p1` and `p2 = rotPart i p1` specialized simultaneously, and `nt`
  a bound on the number of matches of `p1` in `rt1`, and `p2` in `rt2`, respectively.
* `incr_nth v i` (math-comp `seq`) → `incrNth v i`: increment the `i`-th item of `v`, padding
  `v` with zeros if needed.
* `tally_hubcap hc` → `tallyHubcap hc`: the multiset of indices appearing in `hc`, represented
  as `v : List ℕ` such that `v.getD i 0` is the number of times `i` appears in `hc` (and `v`
  does not end with `0`).
* `hubcap_cover_rec v b hc` → `hubcapCoverRec v b hc`: the recursive subpredicate for
  `hubcapCover`; `v` is the result of `tallyHubcap` for the original hubcap, and `-b` is the
  upper bound for the sum of the bounds in `hc`, with bounds of constraints on uniquely-covered
  indices doubled.
* `hubcap_cover nhub hc` → `hubcapCover nhub hc`: the hubcap `hc` covers every index
  `i < nhub`, uniquely except for dual constraints with two twice-covered indices, and any dart
  `x` that satisfies the constraints in `hc` must have a non-positive `dscore`.
* `hubcap_rot nhub j p` → `hubcapRot nhub j p`: the rotation of `p` (of size `nhub`) that aligns
  with the rules at position `j`, i.e., a rotation of `j - 2 [mod nhub]`.
* `hub_subn nhub i j` → `hubSubn nhub i j`: `i - j [mod nhub]`.
* `hubcap_fit redp rf p hc` → `hubcapFit redp rf p hc`: any `x` that fits part `p` (of size
  `nhub`) must satisfy all the score constraints in the hubcap `hc`, for `rf`.

## Lemmas (Coq name → Lean name)

`check_dbound1P`, `check_unfitP`, `check_dbound2P`, `check_2dbound2P`, `fit_hubcap_rot`,
`iter_hub_subn` and `hubcap_fit_bound` keep their Coq names, in `namespace FourColor.Hypermap`
(dot notation `G.check_dbound1P`, ...); `hub_subn_hub` and `nth_incr_nth` (math-comp, stated
with `getD`) are in `namespace FourColor`.

## Porting notes

* The checking functions (`checkDbound1Rec`, `checkDbound1`, `checkUnfit`, `checkDbound2Rec`,
  `checkDbound2`, `check2Dbound2Rec`, `check2Dbound2`, `incrNth`, `tallyHubcap`,
  `hubcapCoverRec`, `hubcapCover`, `hubcapRot`, `hubSubn`, `hubcapFit`) are first-order and
  structurally recursive (the recursive ones are annotated `termination_by structural`, on the
  fuel `m` for the `...Rec` checks, as in Coq), so that they can be evaluated by the Lean kernel
  (`decide +kernel`). They follow the Coq definitions literally: the Coq
  `let: SortDrules n r := sort_drules p rs` are `match`es on `SortDrulesResult.mk`, the Coq
  tests `if n is n'.+1 then ... else ...` are `match`es on `ℕ`, `if z isn't Posz n then ...` is
  a `match` on the constructors of `ℤ`, `let: DruleFork rs rt _ := rf` is the pair of
  projections `rf.sourceDrules`, `rf.targetDrules`, `nth 0 v i` is `v.getD i 0`, `0 \notin v`
  is `!v.contains 0`, the natural multiples `b *+ n` of math-comp are the products `b * n` in
  `ℤ`, and `(n_i == 1).+1` is `(n_i == 1).toNat + 1`.
* The Coq section variables `nhub`, `redp`, `rf` and `G`, and the section hypotheses
  `geoG : plain_cubic_pentagonal G` and `redpP` are explicit or implicit arguments of the
  definitions and lemmas that use them (as after the Coq section is closed). `redpP` is stated
  as `∀ x p, redp p = true → G.exactFitp x p = false` (Coq `~~ exact_fitp x p`), and the
  conclusion `~~ exact_fitp x p` of `hubcap_fit_bound` is `G.exactFitp x p = false`.
  `check_dbound1P`, `check_unfitP` and `check_dbound2P` hold in any hypermap; the other lemmas
  assume `[Finite D]` (Coq hypermaps are finite), and `hubcap_fit_bound` `[Fintype D]`, as
  `dscore` sums over a face. The hypothesis `arity x = nhub` of `check_dbound1P` and
  `check_dbound2P` is unused (also in Coq); it is kept, as `_nFx`, to keep the Coq statements.
* The proof of `hubcap_fit_bound` reindexes the sums over the face of `x` by the iterates of
  `face` from `inv_face2 x` (Coq uses `findex`); otherwise it follows the Coq proof (the partial
  tallies `w` and their weighted sums `sum_db2 w`).
-/

namespace FourColor

universe u

/-! ### The hubcap type -/

/-- Coq `hubcap`: the representation type for constraints on `dscore2` values around a given
face. The sequence structure of hubcaps is compressed (the constraint list and the constraints
are merged into one type). -/
inductive Hubcap : Type where
  /-- Coq `Hubcap0`: the empty hubcap. -/
  | nil
  /-- Coq `Hubcap1 j b hc`: the constraint `dscore2 (face^j x) ≤ b` (Coq concrete syntax
  `$[j+1] <= b`), followed by `hc`. -/
  | cons1 (j : ℕ) (b : ℤ) (hc : Hubcap)
  /-- Coq `Hubcap2 j1 j2 b hc`: the constraint `dscore2 (face^j1 x) + dscore2 (face^j2 x) ≤ b`
  (Coq concrete syntax `$[j1+1, j2+1] <= b`), followed by `hc`. -/
  | cons2 (j1 j2 : ℕ) (b : ℤ) (hc : Hubcap)
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr, Inhabited

/-! ### Source bound checking -/

/-- Coq `check_dbound1_rec redp p rs ns m`: the recursive subpredicate of `checkDbound1`; `m` is
a termination count, `p` the intersection of the initial part with some source rules assumed to
match, `rs` the list of rules that overlap with `p` properly, and `ns` the strict bound on the
number of rules in `rs` that can match; `redp` must hold whenever `ns` is reached. -/
def checkDbound1Rec (redp : Part → Bool) (p : Part) (rs : Drules) (ns : ℕ) : ℕ → Bool
  | 0 => false
  | m' + 1 =>
    match rs with
    | r :: rs' =>
      if rs'.length < ns then true else
      let p' := meetPart p r
      (match sortDrules p' rs' with
        | ⟨dns, rs''⟩ =>
          match ns - dns with
          | ns' + 1 => checkDbound1Rec redp p' rs'' ns' m'
          | 0 => redp p') &&
        checkDbound1Rec redp p rs' ns m'
    | [] => true
termination_by structural m => m

/-- Coq `check_dbound1 redp rf p ns`: at most `ns` source rules of `rf` apply at a dart `x` that
fits `p` (if `p` has size `nhub`), i.e., `dbound1 rs0 x ≤ ns`. -/
def checkDbound1 {nhub : ℕ} (redp : Part → Bool) (rf : DruleFork nhub) (p : Part) (ns : ℕ) :
    Bool :=
  checkDbound1Rec redp p rf.sourceDrules ns (rf.sourceDrules.length + 1)

namespace Hypermap

variable {D : Type u} (G : Hypermap D) {nhub : ℕ}

/-- The induction of Coq `check_dbound1P`. -/
private theorem checkDbound1Rec_sound {redp : Part → Bool}
    (redpP : ∀ (x : D) (p : Part), redp p = true → G.exactFitp x p = false) (x : D) :
    ∀ (m ns : ℕ) (rs : Drules) (p : Part), G.exactFitp x p = true →
      checkDbound1Rec redp p rs ns m = true → G.dbound1 rs x ≤ ns := by
  intro m
  induction m with
  | zero => intro ns rs p _ h; simp [checkDbound1Rec] at h
  | succ m ih =>
    intro ns rs p fit_xp h
    cases rs with
    | nil => simp [dbound1]
    | cons r rs =>
      simp only [checkDbound1Rec] at h
      by_cases hlt : rs.length < ns
      · have := List.countP_le_length (p := G.fitp x) (l := rs)
        simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons]
        split <;> omega
      · rw [ite_eq_right hlt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
        obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := h
        by_cases fit_xr : G.fitp x r = true
        · have Efit_p1 : G.exactFitp x (meetPart p r) = true :=
            G.exact_fitp_meet p r x fit_xp fit_xr
          have fit_p1 : G.fitp x (meetPart p r) = true := by
            simp only [exactFitp, Bool.and_eq_true] at Efit_p1
            exact Efit_p1.2
          have hs := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_p1 rs
          revert h1 hs
          rcases sortDrules (meetPart p r) rs with ⟨dns, rs1⟩
          intro h1 hs
          simp only at h1 hs
          revert h1
          rcases hns : ns - dns with _ | ns1
          · intro h1
            rw [redpP x _ h1] at Efit_p1
            exact absurd Efit_p1 (by decide)
          · intro h1
            have := ih ns1 rs1 _ Efit_p1 h1
            simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons, fit_xr, ite_true] at hs this ⊢
            omega
        · have := ih ns rs p fit_xp h2
          simp only [Bool.not_eq_true] at fit_xr
          simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons, fit_xr] at this ⊢
          simpa using this

/-- Coq `check_dbound1P`. -/
theorem check_dbound1P {redp : Part → Bool} {rf : DruleFork nhub}
    (redpP : ∀ (x : D) (p : Part), redp p = true → G.exactFitp x p = false) {x : D} {p : Part}
    {ns : ℕ} (_nFx : G.arity x = nhub) (fit_xp : G.exactFitp x p = true)
    (h : checkDbound1 redp rf p ns = true) : G.dbound1 rf.sourceDrules x ≤ ns :=
  G.checkDbound1Rec_sound redpP x _ ns _ p fit_xp h

end Hypermap

/-- Coq `check_unfit p ru`: part `p` implies one of the "excluded" rules in `ru`. -/
def checkUnfit (p : Part) : Drules → Bool
  | r :: ru' =>
    match cmpPart p r with
    | .subset => true
    | _ => checkUnfit p ru'
  | [] => false
termination_by structural ru => ru

namespace Hypermap

variable {D : Type u} (G : Hypermap D)

/-- Coq `check_unfitP`. -/
theorem check_unfitP {x : D} {p : Part} (fit_xp : G.fitp x p = true) :
    ∀ ru : Drules, G.dbound1 ru x = 0 → checkUnfit p ru = false := by
  intro ru
  induction ru with
  | nil => intro _; rfl
  | cons r ru ih =>
    intro h
    have hr := G.fitp_cmp p x fit_xp r
    simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons] at h
    have fit_xr : G.fitp x r = false := by
      by_contra hne
      simp only [Bool.not_eq_false] at hne
      simp [hne] at h
    have h' : G.dbound1 ru x = 0 := by
      simp only [fit_xr, Bool.false_eq_true, ite_false, Nat.add_zero] at h
      exact h
    simp only [checkUnfit]
    rcases hc : cmpPart p r
    · exact ih h'
    · exact ih h'
    · rw [hc, fit_xr] at hr
      simp [applyPartRel] at hr

end Hypermap

/-! ### Single target bound checking -/

/-- Coq `check_dbound2_rec redp p rt rs ru nt m`: the recursive subpredicate of `checkDbound2`;
the parameters are as for `checkDbound1Rec`, except that we also keep track of the target rules
`rt`, the bound `nt` is for target rules, `p` is specialized according to target rules, and `ru`
is the list of target rules that have been assumed NOT to match. -/
def checkDbound2Rec (redp : Part → Bool) (p : Part) (rt rs ru : Drules) (nt : ℕ) : ℕ → Bool
  | 0 => false
  | m' + 1 =>
    match rt with
    | [] => true
    | r :: rt' =>
      if rt'.length < nt then true else
      let p' := meetPart p r
      (if checkUnfit p' ru then true else
        match sortDrules p' rt' with
        | ⟨dnt, rt''⟩ =>
          match sortDrules p' rs with
          | ⟨dns, rs'⟩ =>
            match dns + nt - dnt with
            | nt' + 1 => checkDbound2Rec redp p' rt'' rs' ru nt' m'
            | 0 => redp p') &&
        checkDbound2Rec redp p rt' rs (r :: ru) nt m'
termination_by structural m => m

/-- Coq `check_dbound2 redp rf p b`: the net score transfer for a dart `x` that fits part `p`
(of size `nhub`), under the rules of `rf`, is at most `b`; more precisely,
`dbound2 rt0 rs0 x ≤ b`. -/
def checkDbound2 {nhub : ℕ} (redp : Part → Bool) (rf : DruleFork nhub) (p : Part) (b : ℤ) :
    Bool :=
  match sortDrules p rf.targetDrules with
  | ⟨dnt, rt'⟩ =>
    match sortDrules p rf.sourceDrules with
    | ⟨dns, rs'⟩ =>
      match (dns : ℤ) - (dnt : ℤ) + b with
      | .ofNat nt => checkDbound2Rec redp p rt' rs' [] nt (rt'.length + 2)
      | .negSucc _ => false

namespace Hypermap

variable {D : Type u} (G : Hypermap D) {nhub : ℕ}

/-- The induction of Coq `check_dbound2P`. -/
private theorem checkDbound2Rec_sound {redp : Part → Bool}
    (redpP : ∀ (x : D) (p : Part), redp p = true → G.exactFitp x p = false) (x : D) :
    ∀ (m nt : ℕ) (rt rs ru : Drules) (p : Part), G.exactFitp x p = true →
      G.dbound1 ru x = 0 → checkDbound2Rec redp p rt rs ru nt m = true →
      G.dbound1 rt x ≤ nt + G.dbound1 rs x := by
  intro m
  induction m with
  | zero => intro nt rt rs ru p _ _ h; simp [checkDbound2Rec] at h
  | succ m ih =>
    intro nt rt rs ru p Exp bound_ru h
    cases rt with
    | nil => simp [dbound1]
    | cons r rt =>
      simp only [checkDbound2Rec] at h
      by_cases hlt : rt.length < nt
      · have := List.countP_le_length (p := G.fitp x) (l := rt)
        simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons]
        split <;> omega
      · rw [ite_eq_right hlt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
        obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := h
        by_cases fit_xr : G.fitp x r = true
        · have Exp1 : G.exactFitp x (meetPart p r) = true := G.exact_fitp_meet p r x Exp fit_xr
          have fit_xp1 : G.fitp x (meetPart p r) = true := by
            simp only [exactFitp, Bool.and_eq_true] at Exp1
            exact Exp1.2
          rw [G.check_unfitP fit_xp1 ru bound_ru] at h1
          have hst := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_xp1 rt
          have hss := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_xp1 rs
          revert h1 hst hss
          rcases sortDrules (meetPart p r) rt with ⟨dnt, rt1⟩
          rcases sortDrules (meetPart p r) rs with ⟨dns, rs1⟩
          intro h1 hst hss
          simp only [Bool.false_eq_true, ite_false] at h1 hst hss
          revert h1
          rcases hnt : dns + nt - dnt with _ | nt1
          · intro h1
            rw [redpP x _ h1] at Exp1
            exact absurd Exp1 (by decide)
          · intro h1
            have := ih nt1 rt1 rs1 ru _ Exp1 bound_ru h1
            simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons, fit_xr, ite_true] at hst hss this ⊢
            omega
        · simp only [Bool.not_eq_true] at fit_xr
          have bound_ru' : G.dbound1 (r :: ru) x = 0 := by
            simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons, fit_xr] at bound_ru ⊢
            simpa using bound_ru
          have := ih nt rt rs (r :: ru) p Exp bound_ru' h2
          simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons, fit_xr] at this ⊢
          simpa using this

/-- Coq `check_dbound2P`. -/
theorem check_dbound2P {redp : Part → Bool} {rf : DruleFork nhub}
    (redpP : ∀ (x : D) (p : Part), redp p = true → G.exactFitp x p = false) {x : D} {p : Part}
    {b : ℤ} (_nFx : G.arity x = nhub) (Exp : G.exactFitp x p = true)
    (h : checkDbound2 redp rf p b = true) :
    G.dbound2 rf.targetDrules rf.sourceDrules x ≤ b := by
  have fit_xp : G.fitp x p = true := by
    simp only [exactFitp, Bool.and_eq_true] at Exp
    exact Exp.2
  have hst := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_xp rf.targetDrules
  have hss := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_xp rf.sourceDrules
  unfold checkDbound2 at h
  unfold dbound2
  revert h hst hss
  rcases sortDrules p rf.targetDrules with ⟨dnt, rt⟩
  rcases sortDrules p rf.sourceDrules with ⟨dns, rs⟩
  intro h hst hss
  simp only at h hst hss
  rw [hst, hss]
  revert h
  rcases hb : (dns : ℤ) - (dnt : ℤ) + b with nt | _
  · intro h
    have := G.checkDbound2Rec_sound redpP x _ nt rt rs [] p Exp rfl h
    rw [Int.ofNat_eq_natCast] at hb
    push_cast
    omega
  · intro h
    simp at h

end Hypermap

/-! ### Dual target bound check -/

/-- Coq `check_2dbound2_rec nhub redp p1 p2 rt1 rs1 ru1 rt2 rs2 ru2 i nt m`: the recursive
subpredicate of `check2Dbound2`; the parameters are as for `checkDbound2Rec`, with both `p1` and
`p2 = rotPart i p1` specialized simultaneously, and `nt` a bound on the number of matches of
`p1` in `rt1`, and `p2` in `rt2`, respectively. -/
def check2Dbound2Rec (nhub : ℕ) (redp : Part → Bool) (p1 p2 : Part)
    (rt1 rs1 ru1 rt2 rs2 ru2 : Drules) (i nt : ℕ) : ℕ → Bool
  | 0 => false
  | m' + 1 =>
    match rt1 with
    | [] =>
      match rt2 with
      | [] => true
      | _ :: _ => check2Dbound2Rec nhub redp p2 p1 rt2 rs2 ru2 rt1 rs1 ru1 (nhub - i) nt m'
    | r :: rt1' =>
      if rt1'.length + rt2.length < nt then true else
      let p1' := meetPart p1 r
      let p2' := rotPart i p1'
      (if checkUnfit p1' ru1 || checkUnfit p2' ru2 then true else
        match sortDrules p1' rt1' with
        | ⟨dnt1, rt1''⟩ =>
          match sortDrules p1' rs1 with
          | ⟨dns1, rs1'⟩ =>
            match sortDrules p2' rt2 with
            | ⟨dnt2, rt2'⟩ =>
              match sortDrules p2' rs2 with
              | ⟨dns2, rs2'⟩ =>
                match dns1 + (dns2 + nt) - (dnt1 + dnt2) with
                | nt' + 1 =>
                  check2Dbound2Rec nhub redp p1' p2' rt1'' rs1' ru1 rt2' rs2' ru2 i nt' m'
                | 0 => redp p1') &&
        check2Dbound2Rec nhub redp p1 p2 rt1' rs1 (r :: ru1) rt2 rs2 ru2 i nt m'
termination_by structural m => m

/-- Coq `check_2dbound2 redp rf p1 i b`: the sum of the net score transfers for a dart `x` that
fits part `p1` (of size `nhub`), and for `y = face^i x`, is at most `b`:
`dbound2 rt0 rs0 x + dbound2 rt0 rs0 y ≤ b`. -/
def check2Dbound2 {nhub : ℕ} (redp : Part → Bool) (rf : DruleFork nhub) (p1 : Part) (i : ℕ)
    (b : ℤ) : Bool :=
  let p2 := rotPart i p1
  match sortDrules p1 rf.targetDrules with
  | ⟨dnt1, rt1⟩ =>
    match sortDrules p1 rf.sourceDrules with
    | ⟨dns1, rs1⟩ =>
      match sortDrules p2 rf.targetDrules with
      | ⟨dnt2, rt2⟩ =>
        match sortDrules p2 rf.sourceDrules with
        | ⟨dns2, rs2⟩ =>
          match ((dns1 + dns2 : ℕ) : ℤ) - ((dnt1 + dnt2 : ℕ) : ℤ) + b with
          | .ofNat nt =>
            let m := rt1.length + (rt2.length + 3)
            check2Dbound2Rec nhub redp p1 p2 rt1 rs1 [] rt2 rs2 [] i nt m
          | .negSucc _ => false

namespace Hypermap

variable {D : Type u} (G : Hypermap D) {nhub : ℕ}

/-- The induction of Coq `check_2dbound2P`: `x2 = face^i x1` fits `p2`, and the roles of the two
darts are swapped when the target rules of the first one are exhausted. -/
private theorem check2Dbound2Rec_sound [Finite D] {redp : Part → Bool}
    (redpP : ∀ (x : D) (p : Part), redp p = true → G.exactFitp x p = false) :
    ∀ (m nt : ℕ) (x1 : D) (i : ℕ) (p1 p2 : Part) (rt1 rs1 ru1 rt2 rs2 ru2 : Drules),
      G.arity x1 = nhub → i ≤ nhub →
      G.exactFitp x1 p1 = true → G.exactFitp (G.face^[i] x1) p2 = true →
      G.dbound1 ru1 x1 = 0 → G.dbound1 ru2 (G.face^[i] x1) = 0 →
      check2Dbound2Rec nhub redp p1 p2 rt1 rs1 ru1 rt2 rs2 ru2 i nt m = true →
      G.dbound1 rt1 x1 + G.dbound1 rt2 (G.face^[i] x1) ≤
        nt + (G.dbound1 rs1 x1 + G.dbound1 rs2 (G.face^[i] x1)) := by
  intro m
  induction m with
  | zero =>
    intro nt x1 i p1 p2 rt1 rs1 ru1 rt2 rs2 ru2 _ _ _ _ _ _ h
    simp [check2Dbound2Rec] at h
  | succ m ih =>
    intro nt x1 i p1 p2 rt1 rs1 ru1 rt2 rs2 ru2 nFx1 ub_i Exp1 Exp2 b1ru1 b1ru2 h
    cases rt1 with
    | nil =>
      cases rt2 with
      | nil => simp [dbound1]
      | cons r2 rt2 =>
        simp only [check2Dbound2Rec] at h
        have hx : G.face^[nhub - i] (G.face^[i] x1) = x1 := by
          rw [← Function.iterate_add_apply, Nat.sub_add_cancel ub_i, ← nFx1, G.iter_face_arity]
        have nFx2 : G.arity (G.face^[i] x1) = nhub := by rw [G.arity_iter_face, nFx1]
        have := ih nt (G.face^[i] x1) (nhub - i) p2 p1 (r2 :: rt2) rs2 ru2 [] rs1 ru1 nFx2
          (Nat.sub_le _ _) Exp2 (by rw [hx]; exact Exp1) b1ru2 (by rw [hx]; exact b1ru1) h
        rw [hx] at this
        omega
    | cons r rt1 =>
      simp only [check2Dbound2Rec] at h
      by_cases hlt : rt1.length + rt2.length < nt
      · have h1 := List.countP_le_length (p := G.fitp x1) (l := rt1)
        have h2 := List.countP_le_length (p := G.fitp (G.face^[i] x1)) (l := rt2)
        simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons]
        split <;> omega
      · rw [ite_eq_right hlt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
        obtain ⟨hA, hB⟩ := h
        by_cases fit_r : G.fitp x1 r = true
        · have Exp11 : G.exactFitp x1 (meetPart p1 r) = true :=
            G.exact_fitp_meet p1 r x1 Exp1 fit_r
          have hsz : sizePart (meetPart p1 r) = nhub := by
            simp only [exactFitp, Bool.and_eq_true, beq_iff_eq] at Exp11
            omega
          have Exp21 : G.exactFitp (G.face^[i] x1) (rotPart i (meetPart p1 r)) = true := by
            rw [← G.fitp_rot i _ (by omega) x1]
            exact Exp11
          have fit_p11 : G.fitp x1 (meetPart p1 r) = true := by
            simp only [exactFitp, Bool.and_eq_true] at Exp11
            exact Exp11.2
          have fit_p21 : G.fitp (G.face^[i] x1) (rotPart i (meetPart p1 r)) = true := by
            simp only [exactFitp, Bool.and_eq_true] at Exp21
            exact Exp21.2
          rw [G.check_unfitP fit_p11 ru1 b1ru1, G.check_unfitP fit_p21 ru2 b1ru2] at hA
          have hst1 := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_p11 rt1
          have hss1 := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_p11 rs1
          have hst2 := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_p21 rt2
          have hss2 := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_p21 rs2
          revert hA hst1 hss1 hst2 hss2
          rcases sortDrules (meetPart p1 r) rt1 with ⟨dnt1, rt1'⟩
          rcases sortDrules (meetPart p1 r) rs1 with ⟨dns1, rs1'⟩
          rcases sortDrules (rotPart i (meetPart p1 r)) rt2 with ⟨dnt2, rt2'⟩
          rcases sortDrules (rotPart i (meetPart p1 r)) rs2 with ⟨dns2, rs2'⟩
          intro hA hst1 hss1 hst2 hss2
          simp only [Bool.or_false, Bool.false_eq_true, ite_false] at hA hst1 hss1 hst2 hss2
          revert hA
          rcases hnt : dns1 + (dns2 + nt) - (dnt1 + dnt2) with _ | nt1
          · intro hA
            rw [redpP x1 _ hA] at Exp11
            exact absurd Exp11 (by decide)
          · intro hA
            have := ih nt1 x1 i _ _ rt1' rs1' ru1 rt2' rs2' ru2 nFx1 ub_i Exp11 Exp21 b1ru1
              b1ru2 hA
            simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons, fit_r, ite_true] at hst1 hss1 hst2 hss2 this ⊢
            omega
        · simp only [Bool.not_eq_true] at fit_r
          have b1ru1' : G.dbound1 (r :: ru1) x1 = 0 := by
            simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons, fit_r] at b1ru1 ⊢
            simpa using b1ru1
          have := ih nt x1 i p1 p2 rt1 rs1 (r :: ru1) rt2 rs2 ru2 nFx1 ub_i Exp1 Exp2 b1ru1'
            b1ru2 hB
          simp only [dbound1, List.countP_cons, fit_r] at this ⊢
          simpa using this

/-- Coq `check_2dbound2P`. -/
theorem check_2dbound2P [Finite D] {redp : Part → Bool} {rf : DruleFork nhub}
    (redpP : ∀ (x : D) (p : Part), redp p = true → G.exactFitp x p = false) {x : D} {p : Part}
    {i : ℕ} {b : ℤ} (nFx : G.arity x = nhub) (Exp : G.exactFitp x p = true) (ub_i : i ≤ nhub)
    (h : check2Dbound2 redp rf p i b = true) :
    G.dbound2 rf.targetDrules rf.sourceDrules x +
      G.dbound2 rf.targetDrules rf.sourceDrules (G.face^[i] x) ≤ b := by
  have Ep : sizePart p = nhub := by
    simp only [exactFitp, Bool.and_eq_true, beq_iff_eq] at Exp
    omega
  have Exp2 : G.exactFitp (G.face^[i] x) (rotPart i p) = true := by
    rw [← G.fitp_rot i p (by omega) x]
    exact Exp
  have fit_p1 : G.fitp x p = true := by
    simp only [exactFitp, Bool.and_eq_true] at Exp
    exact Exp.2
  have fit_p2 : G.fitp (G.face^[i] x) (rotPart i p) = true := by
    simp only [exactFitp, Bool.and_eq_true] at Exp2
    exact Exp2.2
  have hst1 := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_p1 rf.targetDrules
  have hss1 := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_p1 rf.sourceDrules
  have hst2 := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_p2 rf.targetDrules
  have hss2 := G.sort_dbound1_eq fit_p2 rf.sourceDrules
  simp only [check2Dbound2] at h
  unfold dbound2
  revert h hst1 hss1 hst2 hss2
  rcases sortDrules p rf.targetDrules with ⟨dnt1, rt1⟩
  rcases sortDrules p rf.sourceDrules with ⟨dns1, rs1⟩
  rcases sortDrules (rotPart i p) rf.targetDrules with ⟨dnt2, rt2⟩
  rcases sortDrules (rotPart i p) rf.sourceDrules with ⟨dns2, rs2⟩
  intro h hst1 hss1 hst2 hss2
  simp only at h hst1 hss1 hst2 hss2
  rw [hst1, hss1, hst2, hss2]
  revert h
  rcases hb : ((dns1 + dns2 : ℕ) : ℤ) - ((dnt1 + dnt2 : ℕ) : ℤ) + b with nt | _
  · intro h
    have := G.check2Dbound2Rec_sound redpP _ nt x i p (rotPart i p) rt1 rs1 [] rt2 rs2 [] nFx
      ub_i Exp Exp2 rfl rfl h
    rw [Int.ofNat_eq_natCast] at hb
    push_cast at hb ⊢
    omega
  · intro h
    simp at h

end Hypermap

/-! ### Cover checking

We compute the multiset of indices in a first pass, then check coverage. -/

/-- math-comp `incr_nth v i`: `v` with its `i`-th item incremented, padding `v` with zeros
(math-comp `ncons i 0 [:: 1]` is `List.replicate i 0 ++ [1]`). -/
def incrNth : List ℕ → ℕ → List ℕ
  | n :: v', i' + 1 => n :: incrNth v' i'
  | n :: v', 0 => (n + 1) :: v'
  | [], i => List.replicate i 0 ++ [1]
termination_by structural _ i => i

/-- math-comp `nth_incr_nth`. -/
theorem nth_incr_nth (v : List ℕ) (i j : ℕ) :
    (incrNth v i).getD j 0 = (if i = j then 1 else 0) + v.getD j 0 := by
  induction v generalizing i j with
  | nil =>
    simp only [incrNth, List.getD_nil, Nat.add_zero]
    induction i generalizing j with
    | zero => cases j <;> simp
    | succ i ih =>
      cases j with
      | zero => simp [List.replicate_succ]
      | succ j =>
        rw [List.replicate_succ, List.cons_append, List.getD_cons_succ, ih]
        simp
  | cons n v ih =>
    cases i with
    | zero => cases j <;> simp [incrNth, Nat.add_comm]
    | succ i =>
      cases j with
      | zero => simp [incrNth]
      | succ j =>
        rw [incrNth, List.getD_cons_succ, List.getD_cons_succ, ih]
        simp

/-- Coq `tally_hubcap hc`: the multiset of indices appearing in `hc`, represented as
`v : List ℕ` such that `v.getD i 0` is the number of times `i` appears in `hc` (and `v` does not
end with `0`). -/
def tallyHubcap : Hubcap → List ℕ
  | .cons1 i _ hc' => incrNth (tallyHubcap hc') i
  | .cons2 i j _ hc' => incrNth (incrNth (tallyHubcap hc') i) j
  | .nil => []
termination_by structural hc => hc

/-- Coq `hubcap_cover_rec v b hc`: the recursive subpredicate of `hubcapCover`; `v` is the result
of `tallyHubcap` for the original hubcap, and `-b` is the upper bound for the sum of the bounds
in `hc`, with bounds of constraints on uniquely-covered indices doubled. -/
def hubcapCoverRec (v : List ℕ) (b : ℤ) (hc : Hubcap) : Bool :=
  match hc with
  | .cons1 i b' hc' =>
    (v.getD i 0 == 1) && hubcapCoverRec v (b' * 2 + b) hc'
  | .cons2 i j b' hc' =>
    let n_i := v.getD i 0
    let n_j := v.getD j 0
    (n_i == n_j) && (decide (n_i ≤ 2) &&
      hubcapCoverRec v (b' * (((n_i == 1).toNat + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + b) hc')
  | .nil =>
    !decide (0 < b)
termination_by structural hc

/-- Coq `hubcap_cover nhub hc`: the hubcap `hc` covers every index `i < nhub`, uniquely except
for dual constraints with two twice-covered indices, and any dart `x` that satisfies the
constraints in `hc` must have a non-positive `dscore`. -/
def hubcapCover (nhub : ℕ) (hc : Hubcap) : Bool :=
  let b := dboundK nhub * 2 - 1
  let v := tallyHubcap hc
  (v.length == nhub) && (!v.contains 0 && hubcapCoverRec v b hc)

/-- Coq `hubcap_rot nhub j p`: the rotation of `p` (of size `nhub`) that aligns with the rules
at position `j`, i.e., a rotation of `j - 2 [mod nhub]`. -/
def hubcapRot (nhub j : ℕ) : Part → Part :=
  rotPart (match j with | j' + 2 => j' | _ => nhub + j - 2)

namespace Hypermap

variable {D : Type u} (G : Hypermap D) {nhub : ℕ}

/-- Coq `fit_hubcap_rot`. -/
theorem fit_hubcap_rot [Finite D] (hG : G.PlainCubicPentagonal) {x : D} {p : Part}
    (nFx : G.arity x = nhub) (fit_xp : G.exactFitp x p = true) {j : ℕ} (ltjn : j < nhub) :
    G.exactFitp (G.face^[j] (G.invFace2 x)) (hubcapRot nhub j p) = true := by
  have n_gt1 : 1 < nhub := by
    have := hG.pentagonal x
    omega
  have Ep : sizePart p = nhub := by
    simp only [exactFitp, Bool.and_eq_true, beq_iff_eq] at fit_xp
    omega
  have hx2 : G.face^[2] (G.invFace2 x) = x := by
    simp only [invFace2, Function.iterate_succ_apply', Function.iterate_zero_apply, G.nodeK]
  have hshift : ∀ k, G.face^[k + 2] (G.invFace2 x) = G.face^[k] x := by
    intro k
    rw [Function.iterate_add_apply, hx2]
  have nFx1 : G.arity (G.invFace2 x) = nhub := by
    rw [← G.arity_iter_face 2, hx2, nFx]
  have key : ∀ k, k ≤ nhub → G.exactFitp (G.face^[k] x) (rotPart k p) = true := by
    intro k hk
    rw [← G.fitp_rot k p (by omega) x]
    exact fit_xp
  rcases j with _ | _ | j
  · have e1 : hubcapRot nhub 0 p = rotPart (nhub - 2) p := rfl
    have e2 : G.face^[0] (G.invFace2 x) = G.face^[nhub - 2] x := by
      rw [← hshift, Nat.sub_add_cancel (by omega : 2 ≤ nhub), ← nFx1, G.iter_face_arity]
      rfl
    rw [e1, e2]
    exact key _ (by omega)
  · have e1 : hubcapRot nhub 1 p = rotPart (nhub - 1) p := by
      show rotPart (nhub + 1 - 2) p = rotPart (nhub - 1) p
      congr 1
    have e2 : G.face^[1] (G.invFace2 x) = G.face^[nhub - 1] x := by
      rw [← hshift, show nhub - 1 + 2 = 1 + nhub by omega, Function.iterate_add_apply, ← nFx1,
        G.iter_face_arity]
    rw [e1, e2]
    exact key _ (by omega)
  · have e1 : hubcapRot nhub (j + 2) p = rotPart j p := rfl
    rw [e1, hshift]
    exact key _ (by omega)

end Hypermap

/-- Coq `hub_subn nhub i j`: `i - j [mod nhub]`. -/
def hubSubn (nhub i j : ℕ) : ℕ := (if j ≤ i then i else i + nhub) - j

/-- Coq `hub_subn_hub`. -/
theorem hub_subn_hub {nhub i : ℕ} (j : ℕ) (ltin : i < nhub) : hubSubn nhub i j ≤ nhub := by
  unfold hubSubn
  split <;> omega

namespace Hypermap

variable {D : Type u} (G : Hypermap D) {nhub : ℕ}

/-- Coq `iter_hub_subn`. -/
theorem iter_hub_subn [Finite D] (i : ℕ) {j : ℕ} (ltjn : j < nhub) (x : D)
    (nFx : G.arity x = nhub) : G.face^[hubSubn nhub i j] (G.face^[j] x) = G.face^[i] x := by
  rw [← Function.iterate_add_apply]
  unfold hubSubn
  split
  · congr 1
    omega
  · rw [show i + nhub - j + j = i + nhub by omega, Function.iterate_add_apply, ← nFx,
      G.iter_face_arity]

end Hypermap

/-- Coq `hubcap_fit redp rf p hc`: any dart `x` that fits part `p` (of size `nhub`) must satisfy
all the score constraints in the hubcap `hc`, for the rules of `rf`. -/
def hubcapFit {nhub : ℕ} (redp : Part → Bool) (rf : DruleFork nhub) (p : Part) (hc : Hubcap) :
    Bool :=
  match hc with
  | .cons1 j b hc' =>
    checkDbound2 redp rf (hubcapRot nhub j p) b && hubcapFit redp rf p hc'
  | .cons2 j1 j2 b hc' =>
    check2Dbound2 redp rf (hubcapRot nhub j1 p) (hubSubn nhub j2 j1) b && hubcapFit redp rf p hc'
  | .nil =>
    true
termination_by structural hc

/-! ### The hubcap bound -/

/-- `getD` within the bounds of a list. -/
private theorem getD_eq_getElem_zero {l : List ℕ} {n : ℕ} (hn : n < l.length) :
    l.getD n 0 = l[n] := by
  rw [List.getD_eq_getElem?_getD, List.getElem?_eq_getElem hn, Option.getD_some]

/-- `getD` beyond the bounds of a list (math-comp `nth_default`). -/
private theorem getD_eq_zero_of_le {l : List ℕ} {n : ℕ} (hn : l.length ≤ n) :
    l.getD n 0 = 0 := by
  rw [List.getD_eq_getElem?_getD, List.getElem?_eq_none hn, Option.getD_none]

/-- The multiplier of the bound at index `i`, for a partial tally `w` of a hubcap of tally `v`
(in the Coq proof of `hubcap_fit_bound`, `db2 w y = b y m` with this multiplier `m` for the index
`i = findex face x1 y`): `0` if `i` does not occur in `w`, `2` if it occurs at least twice, and
`(v_i == 1).+1` if it occurs once. -/
private def tallyWeight (v w : List ℕ) (i : ℕ) : ℤ :=
  if 1 < w.getD i 0 then 2 else if w.getD i 0 < 1 then 0 else if v.getD i 0 = 1 then 2 else 1

/-- Coq `db2_inc` (in `hubcap_fit_bound`): adding one occurrence of `i` to a partial tally. -/
private theorem sum_tallyWeight_incr (n : ℕ) (B : ℕ → ℤ) (v w : List ℕ) (i : ℕ)
    (vb : ∀ k, (incrNth w i).getD k 0 ≤ v.getD k 0) (ltin : i < n) (le2 : v.getD i 0 ≤ 2) :
    ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, tallyWeight v (incrNth w i) k * B k =
      (if v.getD i 0 = 1 then 2 else 1) * B i +
        ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, tallyWeight v w k * B k := by
  have hwi : w.getD i 0 + 1 ≤ v.getD i 0 := by
    have := vb i
    rw [nth_incr_nth, ite_eq_left rfl] at this
    omega
  have hw : ∀ k, tallyWeight v (incrNth w i) k =
      tallyWeight v w k + if k = i then (if v.getD i 0 = 1 then 2 else 1) else 0 := by
    intro k
    unfold tallyWeight
    rw [nth_incr_nth]
    by_cases hki : k = i
    · subst hki
      rw [ite_eq_left rfl, ite_eq_left rfl]
      rcases Nat.lt_or_ge (w.getD k 0) 1 with h0 | h1
      · have h0' : w.getD k 0 = 0 := by omega
        rw [h0']
        simp
      · have h1' : w.getD k 0 = 1 := by omega
        have hv2 : v.getD k 0 = 2 := by omega
        rw [h1', hv2]
        simp
    · rw [ite_eq_right (Ne.symm hki), ite_eq_right hki, Nat.zero_add, add_zero]
  simp only [hw, add_mul, Finset.sum_add_distrib, ite_mul, zero_mul, Finset.sum_ite_eq',
    Finset.mem_range, ltin, ite_true]
  ring

namespace Hypermap

variable {D : Type u} (G : Hypermap D) {nhub : ℕ}

open Classical in
/-- A sum over the face of `x` is a sum over the iterates `face^i x`, `i < arity x`. -/
private theorem sum_cface_iter [Fintype D] (x : D) (F : D → ℤ) :
    ∑ y ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun y => G.cface x y), F y =
      ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (G.arity x), F (G.face^[i] x) := by
  have hper : G.arity x = Function.minimalPeriod G.face x := order_eq_minimalPeriod G.faceI x
  have hinj : Set.InjOn (fun i => G.face^[i] x) ↑(Finset.range (G.arity x)) := by
    rw [Finset.coe_range, hper]
    exact Function.iterate_injOn_Iio_minimalPeriod
  rw [← Finset.sum_image hinj]
  congr 1
  ext y
  simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and, Finset.mem_image, Finset.mem_range]
  constructor
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := fconnect_iff_iterate.1 h
    refine ⟨n % G.arity x, Nat.mod_lt _ (order_pos G.faceI x), ?_⟩
    rw [hper]
    exact Function.iterate_mod_minimalPeriod_eq
  · rintro ⟨i, -, rfl⟩
    exact fconnect_iterate _ _ _

open Classical in
/-- Coq `hubcap_fit_bound`. -/
theorem hubcap_fit_bound [Fintype D] (hG : G.PlainCubicPentagonal) {redp : Part → Bool}
    {rf : DruleFork nhub}
    (redpP : ∀ (x : D) (p : Part), redp p = true → G.exactFitp x p = false) {x : D} {p : Part}
    {hc : Hubcap} (Ep : sizePart p = nhub) (pos_x : 0 < G.dscore x)
    (h : (hubcapCover nhub hc && hubcapFit redp rf p hc) = true) :
    G.exactFitp x p = false := by
  rw [Bool.and_eq_true] at h
  obtain ⟨hcov, hc_p⟩ := h
  simp only [hubcapCover, Bool.and_eq_true, beq_iff_eq, Bool.not_eq_true'] at hcov
  obtain ⟨Ev, v'0, hc_v⟩ := hcov
  rw [← Bool.not_eq_true]
  intro Exp
  -- the hub, as seen from `x1 = face⁻² x`
  have hx2 : G.face^[2] (G.invFace2 x) = x := by
    simp only [invFace2, Function.iterate_succ_apply', Function.iterate_zero_apply, G.nodeK]
  have x1Fx : G.cface (G.invFace2 x) x := by
    have := fconnect_iterate G.face (G.invFace2 x) 2
    rwa [hx2] at this
  have nFx : G.arity x = nhub := by
    simp only [exactFitp, Bool.and_eq_true, beq_iff_eq] at Exp
    omega
  have nFx1 : G.arity (G.invFace2 x) = nhub := by rw [G.arity_cface x1Fx, nFx]
  -- the bound on the scores around the hub
  have cap := G.dscore_cap2 rf hG nFx pos_x
  rw [Finset.filter_congr (fun y _ => (G.same_cface x1Fx y).symm), G.sum_cface_iter,
    nFx1] at cap
  set B : ℕ → ℤ := fun i =>
    G.dbound2 rf.targetDrules rf.sourceDrules (G.face^[i] (G.invFace2 x)) with hB
  set v := tallyHubcap hc with hv
  -- every index is covered
  have hv_pos : ∀ k, k < nhub → 1 ≤ v.getD k 0 := by
    intro k hk
    rw [← Ev] at hk
    rw [getD_eq_getElem_zero hk]
    by_contra h0
    have h0' : v[k] = 0 := by omega
    have hmem : 0 ∈ v := h0' ▸ List.getElem_mem hk
    rw [← List.contains_iff_mem, v'0] at hmem
    exact absurd hmem (by decide)
  have db2v : ∑ k ∈ Finset.range nhub, tallyWeight v v k * B k =
      2 * ∑ k ∈ Finset.range nhub, B k := by
    rw [Finset.mul_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k hk => ?_
    have h1 := hv_pos k (Finset.mem_range.1 hk)
    unfold tallyWeight
    split_ifs <;> first | rfl | omega
  -- the main induction, on the constraints of the hubcap
  have main : ∀ (hc' : Hubcap) (b0 : ℤ), hubcapCoverRec v b0 hc' = true →
      hubcapFit redp rf p hc' = true → (∀ k, (tallyHubcap hc').getD k 0 ≤ v.getD k 0) →
      ∑ k ∈ Finset.range nhub, tallyWeight v (tallyHubcap hc') k * B k ≤ -b0 := by
    intro hc'
    induction hc' with
    | nil =>
      intro b0 hcov _ _
      simp only [hubcapCoverRec, Bool.not_eq_true', decide_eq_false_iff_not, not_lt] at hcov
      have h0 : ∀ k, tallyWeight v (tallyHubcap .nil) k = 0 := by
        intro k
        simp [tallyWeight, tallyHubcap]
      simp only [h0, zero_mul, Finset.sum_const_zero]
      linarith
    | cons1 i b1 hc' ih =>
      intro b0 hcov hfit vb
      simp only [hubcapCoverRec, Bool.and_eq_true, beq_iff_eq] at hcov
      obtain ⟨Dvi, hcov'⟩ := hcov
      simp only [hubcapFit, Bool.and_eq_true] at hfit
      obtain ⟨p_b1, hfit'⟩ := hfit
      simp only [tallyHubcap] at vb ⊢
      have vb' : ∀ k, (tallyHubcap hc').getD k 0 ≤ v.getD k 0 := by
        intro k
        have := vb k
        rw [nth_incr_nth] at this
        omega
      have ltin : i < nhub := by
        by_contra hle
        rw [getD_eq_zero_of_le (by omega)] at Dvi
        exact absurd Dvi (by decide)
      rw [sum_tallyWeight_incr nhub B v _ i vb ltin (by omega), Dvi, ite_eq_left rfl]
      have ih' := ih (b1 * 2 + b0) hcov' hfit' vb'
      have hb1 : B i ≤ b1 :=
        G.check_dbound2P redpP (by rw [G.arity_iter_face, nFx1])
          (G.fit_hubcap_rot hG nFx Exp ltin) p_b1
      linarith
    | cons2 j i b1 hc' ih =>
      intro b0 hcov hfit vb
      simp only [hubcapCoverRec, Bool.and_eq_true, beq_iff_eq, decide_eq_true_eq] at hcov
      obtain ⟨Dvi, vj_le2, hcov'⟩ := hcov
      simp only [hubcapFit, Bool.and_eq_true] at hfit
      obtain ⟨p_b1, hfit'⟩ := hfit
      simp only [tallyHubcap] at vb ⊢
      have vb_j : ∀ k, (incrNth (tallyHubcap hc') j).getD k 0 ≤ v.getD k 0 := by
        intro k
        have := vb k
        rw [nth_incr_nth] at this
        omega
      have vb' : ∀ k, (tallyHubcap hc').getD k 0 ≤ v.getD k 0 := by
        intro k
        have := vb_j k
        rw [nth_incr_nth] at this
        omega
      have vj_gt0 : 0 < v.getD j 0 := by
        have := vb_j j
        rw [nth_incr_nth, ite_eq_left rfl] at this
        omega
      have ltjn : j < nhub := by
        by_contra hle
        rw [getD_eq_zero_of_le (by omega)] at vj_gt0
        exact absurd vj_gt0 (by decide)
      have ltin : i < nhub := by
        by_contra hle
        rw [Dvi, getD_eq_zero_of_le (by omega)] at vj_gt0
        exact absurd vj_gt0 (by decide)
      rw [sum_tallyWeight_incr nhub B v _ i vb ltin (by omega),
        sum_tallyWeight_incr nhub B v _ j vb_j ltjn vj_le2]
      have ih' := ih _ hcov' hfit' vb'
      have hsub := G.check_2dbound2P redpP (x := G.face^[j] (G.invFace2 x))
        (by rw [G.arity_iter_face, nFx1]) (G.fit_hubcap_rot hG nFx Exp ltjn)
        (hub_subn_hub j ltin) p_b1
      rw [G.iter_hub_subn i ltjn _ nFx1] at hsub
      -- `hsub : B j + B i ≤ b1`
      rw [← Dvi]
      by_cases h1 : v.getD j 0 = 1
      · simp only [h1, beq_self_eq_true, Bool.toNat_true, ite_true] at ih' ⊢
        push_cast at ih'
        linarith
      · have h1' : (v.getD j 0 == 1) = false := by simpa using h1
        simp only [h1', Bool.toNat_false, ite_eq_right h1] at ih' ⊢
        push_cast at ih'
        linarith
  have := main hc _ hc_v hc_p (fun _ => le_rfl)
  rw [← hv, db2v] at this
  linarith

end Hypermap

end FourColor
